{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"## Operator-scoped backfill — re-sign only `open` / `in_progress` tickets\n\nOperator decision: repair only the tickets whose attestation may still be consumed by a live\nclaim or close gate. Closed tickets keep the historical gap (bounded, dated, documented above).\n**No force used anywhere.**\n\n### Point 5 first — is the backfill itself affected by this bug?\n\n**Confirmed safe, and for a stronger reason than \"the binding is present\".** Run from the local\nCLI on the operator box:\n\n```\nREBAR_OPCERT_ENV_ID    : None\nREBAR_OPCERT_KEY_PATH  : None\ncurrent_binding()      : None\nkey_path               : /Users/joeoakhart/rebar/.tickets-tracker/.opcert-key  (mtime Aug 26 17:51)\nprincipal              : b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126\nstore .env-id          : b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126   → principal == env-id\nsigning key            : …3vTkZoRYQEdEYIl3nQuh\nprincipal pinned in trusted_environments.yaml : False\n```\n\nThis bug requires principal↔key **divergence**, which requires `REBAR_OPCERT_ENV_ID` to be set\n*without* a matching key. Here **neither** is set, so both halves resolve from the same source —\nthe store's own genesis — and the key is the **pre-existing** one (Aug 26), not freshly\nauto-generated. Because `b8a354e0` is *not* pinned, verification takes the `own_key` branch\nagainst that very key: self-consistent by construction. This is the identical identity the\noperator's original e956 recovery used (`…3vTkZoRYQEdEYIl3nQuh` is the \"GOOD\" embedded key\nextracted in the RCA above).\n\nRun via the **local CLI**, not MCP, deliberately: MCP would sign under `9f1c8e42`, whose\npinned-key path is the one this bug breaks on the still-unfixed remote, and whose code clone\ncannot resolve commits (`009f-5f7f-07a5-4b36`). MCP `summary` also timed out at 300s during this\nwork. The local CLI is the sanctioned fallback and matches how e956 was recovered.\n\n**Caveat, stated plainly:** these certs are certified under `own_key` **on this box**, not as\npinned-environment certs. If `verify.require_environment` is ever flipped on (currently unset —\nADR 0104 decision 3), they would need re-earning. Same property as the original e956 recovery.\n\n### 1. Scope split — 7 of 46 in scope\n\n| status | count | disposition |\n|---|---|---|\n| `closed` | **39** | out of scope — untouched |\n| `in_progress` | **6** | in scope |\n| `open` | **1** | in scope |\n\nOf the 7 in-scope, the **live** baseline (the reducer keeps only the latest cert per kind, so some\nhad already been recovered) showed **5** actually mismatching; `7370` and `aa9e` already certified\nand were left alone.\n\n### 2-3. Per-ticket outcome\n\n| ticket | alias | type | before | `sign-review` | after |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| `1205-63b2-2c01-4e7f` | smudgeless-friendless-longspur | bug | mismatch | **re-signed** | **certified** |\n| `ee2e-6fec-aa8a-4e77` | inanimate-unrideable-wasp | task | mismatch | **re-signed** | **certified** |\n| `6640-ac11-5c55-46b5` | intensive-messy-zethuswasp | story | mismatch | **REFUSED** | mismatch |\n| `a374-849c-c8f2-4234` | yaw-quota-wraith | epic | mismatch | **REFUSED** | mismatch |\n| `d8a3-ff71-8112-4e55` | lettered-depressing-willet | epic | mismatch | **REFUSED** | mismatch |\n| `7370-0274-9f80-437d` | bighearted-broke-mallard | task | certified | not run | certified |\n| `aa9e-3d35-fd3e-41ee` | jaunty-pugnacious-stinkpot | story | certified | not run | certified |\n\n**Refusals, verbatim reasons — all correct behaviour, none forced:**\n\n- **`6640`** — `stale-pin-drift`: *\"a dependency's plan material changed since the review\n  (2164-97a8-ca89-4546)\"*. One child drifted (`6a8860eaecb57974` → `833dc71165418420`); four\n  children and one prerequisite still current.\n- **`a374`** (epic) — `stale-pin-drift`: **three** children drifted (`08ab-60d2-3082-4b47`,\n  `1c52-5e73-4d61-4124`, `afe3-5aec-51cb-4e02`).\n- **`d8a3`** (epic) — plan changed: *\"description (2598 → 2651 chars), children (0 → 1499\n  children)\"*.\n\nThese three need a fresh `rebar review-plan`, and **would have needed one regardless of this\nbug** — the staleness is genuine plan drift, not signature corruption. Not run here: each is a\nbillable 15-20 min gate and that is the operator's call.\n\n### 4. Post-backfill verification\n\n`verify-signature` on all 7, both kinds. The two re-signed tickets flipped **mismatch →\ncertified**; the three refused remain mismatch; the two untouched are unchanged.\n\n**Completion-verifier:** no in-scope ticket has a *mismatching* CV cert — 5 are `unsigned` (no CV\ncert exists) and 2 are `certified` (`aa9e` under `b8a354e0`, `ee2e` under `9f1c8e42`, the latter\nbeing one of the 60 that used the correct pinned key). So no CV remediation was needed, which is\nfortunate: there is no cheap no-LLM re-sign for that kind the way `sign-review` serves plan-review.\n\n**Gate-level check from the MAIN checkout** (`e510c64dbcb6`) — `review-plan --status`, read-only,\nno LLM — because the re-signs were issued from a worktree sitting on an unlanded commit:\n\n```\n1205  ok  certified   verified_at_sha e510c64dbcb6   currency_basis file_impact\nee2e  ok  certified   verified_at_sha e510c64dbcb6   currency_basis fail-safe\n7370  ok  certified   verified_at_sha 6c2267d8d7b1   currency_basis file_impact\naa9e  NOT ok  stale-reopened\n```\n\nThe worktree-HEAD concern is **resolved**: `verified_at_sha` comes from the signed manifest (the\noriginal review's anchor), not from the signing process's HEAD, so re-signing from the debug\nworktree did not anchor anything to an unlanded commit.\n\n**One item needing your attention, unrelated to this bug:** `aa9e-3d35-fd3e-41ee`'s signature\nverifies, but its *gate* verdict is `stale-reopened` — *\"the attestation predates the latest\nreopen (signed 1788495338…, reopened 1788506574…) — reopening resets the attestation, so nothing\nin the plan need have changed.\"* `sign-review` cannot repair that (a reopen is a lifecycle reset,\nnot a signature problem); it needs a fresh review. I did not touch it.\n\n### Net\n\nIn-scope live-gate failures caused by this bug: **2 of 2 repairable are repaired.** The remaining\n3 are blocked on genuine plan drift and need a fresh review. Closed tickets left alone as\ninstructed."},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1788572927983247760,"uuid":"a4ef03a7-cfdf-4d99-b925-45c779c02124"}